    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A man is four times as old as his son. In five years he will be only three times as old as his son. What is the man’s present age?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "40 years.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ years be the son’s present age. The man’s present age is $4x$ years. In five years their ages will be $x+5$ and $4x+5$ years.\n$$\\begin{align*}4x+5&=3(x+5)\\\\4x+5&=3x+15\\\\x&=10\\end{align*}$$\nThe man’s present age is $4\\times10=40$ years.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
